{"parentUuid":"7414e45e-4f7f-490d-82c7-e15a75f6db5a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"04b90b0f-8126-4ccf-bbcf-bbcb2b29a279","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZLeT4GUys7dBeQYNXshyz","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: no-merge-asks-until-finished\ndescription: \"User (2026-10-24) — nothing merges until ALL the work is finished; stop asking about merges/approvals; handle small decisions myself and keep the todo board free of \\\"waiting on you\\\" noise\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5\n  modified: 2026-10-24T16:34:34.360Z\n---\n\nThe user said: *\"I am not merging anything TILL WE FINISH EVERYTHING so stop asking, and on the other stuff you handle it, most is unnecessary and can wait, so clean the slate for me.\"*\n\n**Why:** the board had filled with merge/approve/close asks (brain #350, CI approval for fork PRs, #142 rescope), and that read as nagging. The user wants one merge pass at the very end, not a trickle of asks.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Do not ask for merges, approvals or PR closes. Leave PRs open, and batch them for a single end-of-work handoff.\n- Make the smaller decisions myself (for example rescoping a PR, or which variant to keep) and note them on the board.\n- On the todo board, `owner: user` is only for things that physically need them, like `/compact`. Everything else is `claude`.\n- Deferred work goes to `todo-board.archive.json` with status `deferred`, not onto the live board.\n\nRelated: [[todo-board-standing-instruction]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0b8022c7-9aa3-496e-a144-5f2fd96fa7b4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:29:58.744Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: no-merge-asks-until-finished\ndescription: \"User (2026-10-24) — nothing merges until ALL the work is finished; stop asking about merges/approvals; handle small decisions myself and keep the todo board free of \\\"waiting on you\\\" noise\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type