{"parentUuid":"aa55b927-bd2f-45ea-a37d-d6d2351ff13a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"04b90b0f-8126-4ccf-bbcf-bbcb2b29a279","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011bZt1h5gAJAB2gGvk8P54p","type":"tool_result","content":"=== BRIEF ===\nkeys: ['generated_at', 'task', 'history', 'likely_edit_files', 'likely_test_files', 'likely_files', 'guidance', 'warnings', 'semantic', 'status']\nTASK: add full Windows support to entire-brain: LOCALAPPDATA store path resolution, detached spawn creation flags, processAlive, long path handling\nfacts: 0\n\n=== RECALL: windows store path / data dir decisions ===\n - constraints.filesystem.portability | Capturing directory identity through an open handle was considered for Windows rename verification, but a real Windows probe showed the handle blocks the rename; revisit only with a handle strategy proven to permit renaming.\n - workflow.testing.rules | Using chmod 000 to simulate an unreadable binding failed on Windows because os.Chmod does not prevent reads there, allowing the test to attempt network access; use a directory at the binding path for a portable non-parse read fail\n - constraints.invariants.general | The `reset` command uses content-clearing followed by directory deletion because \"rename\" was tried and failed on Windows due to active file handles (e.g., SQLite/WAL locks).\n - architecture.data.flow | Workspace additions must store absolute paths rather than relative hints to ensure consistent resolution across different working directories during refresh/query/impact operations.\n - constraints.invariants.general | Windows CI runs **prebuilt test binaries from a bundle**, not from package source. Tests that open source files by relative path (e.g. reading `semantic.go` from the working directory) silently pass on Ubuntu and fail on Windows.\n - constraints.invariants.general | The brain store lives inside the plugins directory (not under XDG_DATA_HOME), so setting XDG_DATA_HOME does not isolate the store in test harnesses; every throwaway test permanently writes into the real store.\n - architecture.data.flow | Dedup using `report.Path` failed because it is a per-run timestamped path; use the stable source path instead to ensure idempotency.\n - constraints.invariants.general | `os.Chmod(file, 0o000)` does not make a file unreadable on Windows (only toggles the read-only bit); use a directory at the path instead to get a cross-platform unreadable-binding test.\n - architecture.data.flow | Cap-tuning and semantic-reranking were tried to solve over-contextualization on the full-brain but failed; the issue is retrieval-relevance where topically-similar \"closed-negatives\" out-compete the \"decision\" fact.\n - constraints.invariants.general | The brain store lives inside the plugins directory, not under XDG_DATA_HOME; symlinking the plugin registry de-isolates the brain store — throwaway test repos must copy (not link) the plugins dir to achieve real isolation.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"25a235ff-ac76-43b0-bb24-b6675f369287","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:30:31.943Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== BRIEF ===\nkeys: ['generated_at', 'task', 'history', 'likely_edit_files', 'likely_test_files', 'likely_files', 'guidance', 'warnings', 'semantic', 'status']\nTASK: add full Windows support to entire-brain: LOCALAPPDATA store path resolution, detached spawn creation flags, processAlive, long path handling\nfacts: 0\n\n=== RECALL: windows store path / data dir decisions ===\n - constraints.filesystem.portability | Capturing directory identity through an open handle was considered for Windows rename verification, but a real Windows probe showed the handle blocks the rename; revisit only with a handle strategy proven to permit renaming.\n - workflow.testing.rules | Using chmod 000 to simulate an unreadable binding failed on Windows because os.Chmod does not prevent reads there, allowing the test to attempt network access; use a directory at the binding path for a portable non-parse read fail\n - constraints.invariants.general | The `reset` command uses content-clearing followed by directory deletion because \"rename\" was tried and failed on Windows due to active file handles (e.g., SQLite/WAL locks).\n - architecture.data.flow | Workspace additions must store absolute paths rather than relative hints to ensure consistent resolution across different working directories during refresh/query/impact operations.\n - constraints.invariants.general | Windows CI runs **prebuilt test binaries from a bundle**, not from package source. Tests that open source files by relative path (e.g. reading `semantic.go` from the working directory) silently pass on Ubuntu and fail on Windows.\n - constraints.invariants.general | The brain store lives inside the plugins directory (not under XDG_DATA_HOME), so setting XDG_DATA_HOME does not isolate the store in test harnesses; every throwaway test permanently writes into the real store.\n - architecture.data.flow | Dedup using `report.Path` failed because it is a per-run timestamped path; use the stable source path instead to ensure idempotency.\n - constraints.invariants.general | `os.Chmod(file, 0o000)` does not make a file unreadable on Windows (only toggles the read-only bit); use a directory at the path instead to get a cross-platform unreadable-binding test.\n - architecture.data.flow | Cap-tuning and semantic-reranking were tried to solve over-contextualization on the full-brain but failed; the issue is retrieval-relevance where topically-similar \"closed-negatives\" out-compete the \"decision\" fact.\n - constraints.invariants.general | The brain store lives inside the plugins directory, not under XDG_DATA_HOME; symlinking the plugin registry de-isolates the brain store — throwaway test repos must copy (not link) the plugins dir to achieve real isolation.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7f77c370-a210-4695-81da-3