{"parentUuid":"46836137-60bf-43d8-8677-2f7164c86b36","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwW4aqF3Ynd7rgJin2ZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committing locally so the work is durable — no push, no PR. (No AI attribution footer, per the devenv CLAUDE.md rule.)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_read_input_tokens":406868,"output_tokens":1682,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1682,"cache_read_input_tokens":406868,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a63760d1-bc45-4c71-9fc6-6a7f31242962","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwW4aSvVLzxM1ivsjT4R","requestRef":"9efa5ef0-a1c1-4a46-a3c6-7e9fd0f2f634","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"932b7330-4bfc-47d5-9e26-3b1ec7bb9367","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:03:13.768Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"932b7330-4bfc-47d5-9e26-3b1ec7bb9367","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwW4aqF3Ynd7rgJin2ZW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018zXwm3S3Hu2epLBKskZeDu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@aisprouts.ngo\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\n\nSix Windows defects, found by auditing against origin/main rather than the\nlocal checkouts, which were 1007 commits stale.\n\nStore path: the brain resolved its plugin data root through XDG and\n~/.local/share on every OS, while the host CLI ignores XDG on Windows and\nreads %LOCALAPPDATA%. Dispatched runs were fine because the host sets\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR, but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different,\nempty store and said nothing. Scoped to the data dir only: config, state and\ncache already agree on every OS, and ResolvePluginDirs has 71 callers.\n\nDetached backfill: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP alone does not detach a child\nfrom the console, so closing the terminal killed the background backfill --\nthe one thing spawnDetached exists to prevent. Adds DETACHED_PROCESS, which\nis safe because stdio already points at a log file. Deliberately not\nCREATE_NO_WINDOW, which Microsoft documents as undefined in combination.\n\nProcessAlive: os.FindProcess succeeds for an exited process whose handle is\nstill open, and os.FindProcess holds exactly such a handle, so a finished\nbackfill reported as running forever and backfillRunning would never start\nanother. Uses WaitForSingleObject, which is unambiguous, rather than\nGetExitCodeProcess, whose STILL_ACTIVE is indistinguishable from a real exit\ncode of 259.\n\nAtomic replace: internal/config made a single MoveFileEx attempt while the\nbrainstore twin retried on sharing and lock violations. The duplication is\nforced by Go's internal-package rule, and is now noted as such.\n\ndoctor: warns when the store sits under OneDrive or on a UNC share, where\nSQLite's WAL is unsafe. Environment-scoped, so it never gates a brain check.\n\nCI: the build matrix excluded windows/arm64 from the initial commit with no\nrecorded reason, while release.yml and nightly.yml both ship that target --\nthe one published target never compiled on a pull request.\n\nAlso pins two measured properties that were previously unstated: the export\ntree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, over Win32's 260 limit\nbefore the store root, working only because Go rewrites long absolute paths\nto the \\\\?\\ form; and evidenceHash is CRLF-sensitive by design, so fact\nanchors do not survive the LF/CRLF boundary between machines.\nMSG\necho \"=== commit ===\"\ngit --no-pager log -1 --format='%h %s'\necho \"=== branch / remote state (nothing pushed) ===\"\ngit status -sb | head -3\necho \"unpushed commits vs origin/main: $(git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD)\"\necho \"=== files in commit ===\"\ngit --no-pager show --stat --format='' HEAD","description":"Commit the Windows work locally"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_read_input_tokens":406868,"output_tokens":1682,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1682,"cache_read_input_tokens":406868,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3134},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018zXwm3S3Hu2epLBKskZeDu":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" -c user.email=\"suhaan@aisprouts.ngo\" commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\n\nSix Windows defects, found by auditing against origin/main rather than the\nlocal checkouts, which were 1007 commits stale.\n\nStore path: the brain resolved its plugin data root through XDG and\n~/.local/share on every OS, while the host CLI ignores XDG on Windows and\nreads %LOCALAPPDATA%. Dispatched runs were fine because the host sets\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR, but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different,\nempty store and said nothing. Scoped to the data dir only: config, state and\ncache already agree on every OS, and ResolvePluginDirs has 71 callers.\n\nDetached backfill: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP alone does not detach a child\nfrom the console, so closing the terminal killed the background backfill --\nthe one thing spawnDetached exists to prevent. Adds DETACHED_PROCESS, which\nis safe because stdio already points at a log file. Deliberately not\nCREATE_NO_WINDOW, which Microsoft documents as undefined in combination.\n\nProcessAlive: os.FindProcess succeeds for an exited process whose handle is\nstill open, and os.FindProcess holds exactly such a handle, so a finished\nbackfill reported as running forever and backfillRunning would never start\nanother. Uses WaitForSingleObject, which is unambiguous, rather than\nGetExitCodeProcess, whose STILL_ACTIVE is indistinguishable from a real exit\ncode of 259.\n\nAtomic replace: internal/config made a single MoveFileEx attempt while the\nbrainstore twin retried on sharing and lock violations. The duplication is\nforced by Go's internal-package rule, and is now noted as such.\n\ndoctor: warns when the store sits under OneDrive or on a UNC share, where\nSQLite's WAL is unsafe. Environment-scoped, so it never gates a brain check.\n\nCI: the build matrix excluded windows/arm64 from the initial commit with no\nrecorded reason, while release.yml and nightly.yml both ship that target --\nthe one published target never compiled on a pull request.\n\nAlso pins two measured properties that were previously unstated: the export\ntree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, over Win32's 260 limit\nbefore the store root, working only because Go rewrites long absolute paths\nto the \\\\?\\ form; and evidenceHash is CRLF-sensitive by design, so fact\nanchors do not survive the LF/CRLF boundary between machines.\nMSG\necho \"=== commit ===\"\ngit --no-pager log -1 --format='%h %s'\necho \"=== branch / remote state (nothing pushed) ===\"\ngit status -sb | head -3\necho \"unpushed commits vs origin/main: $(git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD)\"\necho \"=== files in commit ===\"\ngit --no-pager show --stat --format='' HEAD","description":"Commit the Windows work locally"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a63760d1-bc45-4c71-9fc6-6a7f31242962","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwW4aSvVLzxM1ivsjT4R","requestRef":"9efa5ef0-a1c1-4a46-a3c6-7e9fd0f2f634","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2705bea-68a7-4e74-af36-0e763f8efedf","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:03:28.297Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
